Z||000000||ezsurf||05-27-99||08:32 PM||||<br>I have read information about the MAT (Manifold Air Temperature) Sensor which says that moisture & thermal cycling over a period of time can cause the sensor to loose it's accuracy.  Not only does it loose it's accuracy, but it's entire dynamic resistance range shifts in a direction to indicate that the temperature of the air is higher than it actually is.  The ECM compensates by reducing fuel flow to the injectors, causing a loss of performance.  The ECM will not detect any errors in the form of a trouble code, unless the sensor is either totally shorted out or goes open circuit.  My question is; is there any way to test the sensor for accuracy?  Anyone have a clue?  
Z||000001||ka4nkf||05-29-99||08:19 AM||||Mat Sensor Testing- V6 Models Only<br>You Will Need A OHM Meter.<br>(approximate)<br> F       C        OHMS<br>210     100        185<br>160      70        450<br>100      38       1800<br>70       20       3400<br>40        4       7500<br>20       -7      13500<br>0       -18      25000<br>-40     -40     100700<p><p><p><p>210<br>160<br>100<br>70<br>40<br>20<br>0<br>-40
Z||000002||ka4nkf||05-29-99||08:29 AM||||Try This Again. V6 Models Only<br>You Will Need A OHM Meter. <br>  F       C        OHMS        Readings Are <br>                                (approximate)<br> 210     100        185<br> 160      70        450<br> 100      38       1800<br>  70      20       3400<br>  40       4       7500<br>  20      -7      13500<br>   0     -18      25000<br> -40     -40     100700
Z||000003||ka4nkf||05-29-99||08:45 AM||||One More Time ,I Dont Know Why It Dont Print<br>V6 Models Only, And You Will Need A OHM Meter<br>(approximate Readings)<br>210 Degrees Heat You Should Read 185 OHMS<br>160 Degrees Heat You Should Read 450 OHMS<br>100 Degrees Heat You Should Read 1800 OHMS<br> 70 Degrees Heat You Should Read 3400 OHMS<br> 40 Degrees Heat You Should Read 7500 OHMS<br> 20 Degrees Heat You Should Read 13500 OHMS<br>  0 Dwgrees Heat You Should Read 25000 OHMS<br> -40 Degrees Heat You Should Read 100700 OHMS
